From: ProgrammerIn-wonderland <alice@alicesworld.tech>
Subject: [PATCH 9/9] debian.qcom-x1e: Disable stubble UKI packaging

Surface Laptop 7 boots via standard EFI/GRUB and does not use Canonical's
experimental stubble EFI loader. Disabling stubble avoids calling ukify
with unrecognized --hwids arguments and installs standard vmlinuz into
the linux-image package.

Signed-off-by: ProgrammerIn-wonderland <alice@alicesworld.tech>
---
 debian.qcom-x1e/rules.d/arm64.mk | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/debian.qcom-x1e/rules.d/arm64.mk b/debian.qcom-x1e/rules.d/arm64.mk
--- a/debian.qcom-x1e/rules.d/arm64.mk
+++ b/debian.qcom-x1e/rules.d/arm64.mk
@@ -17,6 +17,6 @@ do_tools_rtla = true
 
 do_dtbs		= true
-do_stubble	= true
+do_stubble	= false
 do_skip_checks	= false
 do_zfs		= true
-- 
2.45.0
